        <mxCell id="c29" value="" style="rounded=0;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#5D6D7E;strokeColor=#5D6D7E;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#2C3E50;fontSize=13;fontStyle=0;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="196" y="332" width="364" height="1.5" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c30" value="&lt;i&gt;The excess is the stock of raw materials and packaging at the year-end, 11,751,653.92, less what a target of 28, 60 or 90 days of supply allows at the year&#x27;s rate of issue, 10,161,204.64 a year: 779,489.67, 1,670,335.01 and 2,505,502.51. Even at 90 days the excess is about ten times the year&#x27;s fall in cash. Every bar starts at zero; the months are the excess over a month of issues. An estimate at the year&#x27;s rate of issue, not a forecast of what could be released.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="364" width="860" height="53" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
